This console is not a desktop BSD

`compat.h` defines `__BSD__` from `__FreeBSD__`, and three backends key off it: `gfx_glx`
wants X11, `audio_pulse` wants PulseAudio and `audio_alsa` wants ALSA. This target is
FreeBSD-derived and has none of the three, so it takes SDL for the window, the GL context
and the audio device, which is what upstream's `#else` arms already select.

Without this the payload references all three and the link reports them undefined, because
the sources that define them are excluded for wanting headers this platform has no
equivalent of.

Lifted for `__PROSPERO__` only, so a real BSD build keeps upstream's behaviour exactly.
---
diff --git a/src/pc/compat.h b/src/pc/compat.h
index 8d6a3d4..8315289 100644
--- a/src/pc/compat.h
+++ b/src/pc/compat.h
@@ -1,7 +1,8 @@
 #ifndef COMPAT_H
 #define COMPAT_H value
 
-#if defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__)
+#if (defined(__FreeBSD__) || defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__OpenBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__)) \
+    && !defined(__PROSPERO__)
 #define __BSD__
 #endif
 
